 "waiver_targets": [
  {
   "name": "Caleb Douglas",
   "position": "WR",
   "nfl_team": "MIA",
   "proj": 9.36,
   "ros_rank": 86.0,
   "fp_waiver_rank": 9.0,
   "injury": "ACTIVE",
   "replaces": "Ryan Flournoy",
   "ros_rank_gain": 33.0,
   "week_proj_gain": 0.15,
   "priority": "MEDIUM",
   "availability": "ESPN_WAIVERS",
   "espn_pct_owned": 9.7,
   "fp_waiver_note": "Third-round rookie Caleb Douglas returned from an ankle injury in Week 7 and had 2-70-2 on three targets, scoring on a 63-yard catch-and-run down the left sideline and running a nice in-breaking route to get open for a 7-yard TD catch in the back of the end zone.\n\nDouglas was a standout in Miami's training camp, and he had 5-94-0 on seven targets in Week 1 before going down with the ankle injury in Week 2.\n\nYes, Douglas had only three targets on Sunday. Dolphins QB Malik Willis threw only 21 passes. Miami is low on passing volume most weeks, and that was certainly the case in Week 7.\n\nBut Douglas has been impressive. He could very well emerge as the Dolphins' No. 1 receiver this year. Douglas is a worthwhile upside play."
  },
  {
   "name": "Chig Okonkwo",
   "position": "TE",
   "nfl_team": "WAS",
   "proj": 8.43,
   "ros_rank": 116.0,
   "fp_waiver_rank": 12.0,
