   "week_proj_gain": 1.78,
   "priority": "MEDIUM",
   "availability": "ESPN_WAIVERS",
   "espn_pct_owned": 4.9,
   "fp_waiver_note": "Chig Okonkwo has had 60 or more receiving yards in two straight games, and he had a season-high seven catches on seven targets when we last saw the Commanders in their Week 6 loss to the 49ers.\n\nOkonkwo figures to be an important part of the Commanders' passing game now that Washington's top wide receiver, Terry McLaurin, will miss the rest of the season with a torn patellar tendon.\n\nAlthough he's never had more than 560 receiving yards or three touchdowns in a season since entering the league in 2022, Okonkwo could be poised for his best year to date. He's averaging a career-high 37.5 receiving yards per game and 7.5 yards per target. With good health, Okonkwo could shatter his previous single-season high of 79 targets.\n\nOkonkwo is a solid Week 8 TE option even against an Eagles defense that has allowed the 11th-fewest fantasy points per game to TEs."
  },
