   "fp_waiver_note": "Jets TE Mason Taylor had his finest game of the season Sunday against the Dolphins, with 5-62-2 on six targets. Taylor led the Jets' tight ends in snaps and routes run on Sunday, with rookie first-rounder Kenyon Sadiq playing a limited role. Taylor had one touchdown in 17 previous NFL games, and he hadn't had more than 33 receiving yards in a game before Week 7. Taylor's usage is increasing, so he's worth keeping on the radar, but he isn't worth rostering yet."
